From b96222e3fca070e7403f8a646ea31c2c982dd8d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bench <bench@local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 07:17:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/24] vulkan: PQ2_0 mat-vec: interleave the q8_1 activation
 instead of unpacking 2-bit codes

The mat-vec is instruction-bound on gfx906. (bits >> 2m) & 0x03030303 puts codes m, m+4, m+8, m+12 into byte
lanes, so a q8_1 activation written in that order (quantize_q8_1_x4_i4, mat-vec paths only) feeds v_dot4
directly: 7 instead of ~20 instructions per 16 weights.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
